message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below and credit Azizul Abedin Azmi."
type: software
title: "Bone Age from Hand X-Rays: Sex-Conditioned EfficientNetV2 Regression on the RSNA Pediatric Bone Age Dataset"
authors:
  - given-names: "Azizul Abedin"
    family-names: "Azmi"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-5269-6900"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/azizulabedinazmi/Bone-Age-From-Hand-X-Rays"
url: "https://github.com/azizulabedinazmi/Bone-Age-From-Hand-X-Rays"
abstract: >-
  Regression of pediatric skeletal (bone) age in months from left-hand radiographs of the
  RSNA Pediatric Bone Age dataset, using an EfficientNetV2-S with a learned sex embedding,
  pad-to-square preprocessing and CLAHE, evaluated on a stratified hold-out set and compared
  across a laptop RTX 4060 and a Kaggle GPU.
keywords:
  - bone age assessment
  - pediatric radiology
  - hand X-ray
  - medical imaging
  - deep learning
  - EfficientNetV2
  - RSNA
references:
  - type: article
    title: "The RSNA Pediatric Bone Age Machine Learning Challenge"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Halabi"
        given-names: "Safwan S."
      - name: "et al."
    journal: "Radiology"
    year: 2019
    volume: 290
    issue: 2
    start: 498
    end: 503
